week 4
# RAG Project

## What I set up this week

- Created a Python virtual environment (`venv`)
- Installed project dependencies using `requirements.txt`
- Set up environment variable management using `.env`
- Installed and configured FastAPI and Uvicorn
- Verified backend server runs successfully using Uvicorn
- Confirmed `.env` file loads the `GEMINI_API_KEY` securely

## Purpose of `rag_app.py`

The `rag_app.py` file is the entry point of the backend application.

At this stage, it:
- Loads environment variables from `.env`
- Reads the `GEMINI_API_KEY`
- Confirms the backend server runs using FastAPI
- Provides a `/health` endpoint to verify the server is working

No Gemini or RAG logic has been implemented yet — this file is currently used for environment and server setup validation.

## Questions / Uncertainties

- How the RAG pipeline will be structured in later stages
- How Gemini API will integrate into FastAPI routes
- Best practices for storing embeddings and retrieval logic
- How the backend will scale as features are added